t  a cafe in the city this acts as a useful  vehicle to remind viewers of the current  stakes and context going on in the  special in a natural way  illuminating to us also the very instant  sabo learns about the first place prize  of the tournament  aces flame flame fruit and throughout  this while luffy and the rest of the  pieces get put into place  it's interesting getting to witness  savo's takes on each of the goings-on  leading up to his grand reveal  short as they may be as a fan of the  series i quite enjoyed seeing them  as far as animation goes i found this  film to be surprisingly weak  while the artwork was perfectly fine and  good the animation felt very limited and  clunky  with the vast majority of it barely  moving at all relying heavily on stills  and limited animation i don't think this  would bother many heck i don't think the  vast majority of people out there would  even notice without someone pointing it  out to them if they weren't into  animation in the first place but if you  are someone who enjoys great animation  as a cornerstone to your animated media  maybe sit this one out to cap off this  special there's the moment sabo acquires  the flame flame fruit with additional  dialogue and reflection on what this  means to him  before blasting the floor saving rebecca  and winning the tournament ending  the special overall while i really  didn't love this special by any means i  can at least appreciate the angle with  which it chose to deliver its story  there wasn't a ton of extra stuff added  but what little there was i did enjoy  i don't think i'd recommend this one  over the original series or even as  supplementary material to most  it's really not necessary however if you  love one piece and are looking for  something to tie you over until the next  chapter releases  maybe check it out you could enjoy it  one piece heart of gold  this film starts out pretty much by the  books and the plot itself is really  simple overall there's a little girl of  value on the marine ship  and these pirates want her the pirates  themselves that want this child make up  the villains of the story and while  trying to capture the girls she uses the  chaos that ensues around her capture as  an opportunity to escape  and by pure chance in the vast expanse  of the ocean  who does she run into but the straw hat  crew  that convenient trope aside i do  actually really enjoy this little girl  character she's a little abrasive but  she's tough and that's something a  little different than what i usually see  in these films usually it's nami or  something that needs saving the villain  in this instance is probably the least  interesting villain i've come across in  any of these specials his name is  literally and i quote  mad treasure and he is a treasure hunter  specifically trying to get a hold of  this little girl because she knows where  the pure gold substance is  in this story pure gold is a substance  that can apparently by the entire world  [Laughter]  one major difference i noticed between  these specials is the quality of  animation  implemented and the stories they tell  apart from 3d 2y which was very good and  interesting all of the other specials  are animated in a much more limited  fashion than pretty much any of the  films available for viewing once again  the artwork and character likeness is  perfectly accurate but the movement is  very limited and very little character  acting you don't even need to compare  this to stellar animated features like  movie 6  or any of the modern ones either for  this to be obvious it's clear that the  time dedicated to these wasn't on par  with the films which i suppose is  perfectly fine i guess  films are supposed to be on a larger  scale anyway one thing i will say  regarding the film's approach in terms  of animation is that at the very end of  the film the quality does pick up quite  a bit  thankfully in addition to that the  selection of scenes and settings this  special boasts are interesting too  with a large chunk of this special  taking place in the belly of a giant  anglerfish and in saying that there's  some nice imagery with the giant angler  fish at the end  as well as some nice backgrounds across  the special overall from a story  standpoint  it might be because i've now sat through  so so many  tv specials and films that i've become  jaded of all of these recycled plot  lines  but the story didn't exactly set my  world on fire it has a lot of the same  bells and whistles used in almost any of  the other one-piece films or specials  contrived beginning that hooks the crew  with the main character or villain of  interest  they look for treasure get kidnapped  fight the bad guy at the end and repeat  and while that's a very basic outline a  lot of these specials didn't offer much  in the way of anything significant  branching out from this either  and specifically when it came to these  specials when i don't have really nice  animation to carry me through the film's  unimaginative story  i tend to look more harshly upon it  though i suppose that's my own failing  with that said i genuinely thought that  there were plenty of things  to enjoy about this one and it had at  the very least some interesting  backgrounds and a scrappy kid character  that turned out to be 200 years old  however  having gone through the last month  watching the films and now these tv  specials  i can safely say that they were  significantly better than i anticipated  them to be  now that's not to say that i thought  they were oscar-worthy though i really  did like movie six  i am very impressed nevertheless with  the level of consistency one piece's  back catalog of non-canon material  really has to offer  i was fully prepared to be much more  combative and harsh with my essays but  really none of the films were so bad to  warrant such a criticism and the vast  majority i even enjoyed to a great  extent  the last time i went through a back  catalogu